From 3625030a2b21f5a92a4b5ebbce5607489720ce8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:00:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(picks): one shared start / exit pick mechanism for every
 kind

Record the design of #1448 in docs/decisions/1448-start-exit-shared.md.
Add the shared type camcraft_motion::path_picks (PathPicks, PathPick,
PickRole), the per-kind PickCapability through KindInfo::pick(), the
accessor OpParams::path_picks() and one pick refusal that names the kind,
the pick and the reason. MCP edit_operation names the pick fields, and
list_operation_types says per kind if it takes a pick. Every operation
page draws the Start point and Exit point groups; a kind that does not
take a pick says so by name.

The storage move to one operation-level project key is #3339.

Fixes #3324

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
